WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- All right.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.190
We always like to wrap up with something

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.570
that highlights good in the world.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.764
This is "What I'm Liking."
(vibrant band music)

00:00:05.764 --> 00:00:07.170
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.180
About a year ago I met two sisters,

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.220
doing something simple but extraordinary.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.200
They craft cool origami pieces,

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.610
collect donations for them,

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.920
and use the money to
build fresh water wells

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.210
all over the globe.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.581
In 10 years they have raised
more than $3.5 million.

00:00:21.581 --> 00:00:23.100
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.240
This is incredible.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.800
Now they're busier than ever.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.780
Let's get the founders of Paper for Water

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:28.890
in here for an update.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.517
What's up, Isabelle and Katherine?

00:00:30.517 --> 00:00:32.287
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:33.745
- Hi, Kelly.
- All right, so-

00:00:33.745 --> 00:00:35.340
- Hi, Kelly.
- Hello.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.470
So, ladies, tell us
about your latest well.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.030
Isabelle, we'll start with you.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:42.000
- Yeah, so we were able to build a well

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.910
in Santa Elena, Peru.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.710
This is a super remote community,

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.980
and for decades they hadn't been able

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.120
to build a well there,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.740
because of how remote it is.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.080
And so people were having
to get water from the river,

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.750
which is full of bacteria
and other contaminants.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.090
- Mm.
- And multiple times a day

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.550
people were having to haul
water for their families,

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.110
which meant people couldn't go to work,

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.060
kids couldn't go to school,

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.800
and people were often sick,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.430
so they would have to spend
money on medical costs.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:15.600
But, thanks to the $10,000 we
got on your show last time,

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.550
- Yeah.
- these people now have safe,

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.380
clean, easily accessible water.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.750
- That is so incredible.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.040
Shout out to ATB.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.270
That's how we got that 10 grand.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.340
Oh, my gosh. Catherine, that's just part

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.200
of what you've been up to though, right?

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.033
- Yes.

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:32.700
After being on the show, we
got so many online orders.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.830
We were able to use that money

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.470
for a major project in Kenya,

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.730
at an orphanage.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:41.220
We drilled a deep water well in December

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:44.100
and are now constructing
hand washing stations

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.830
and an elevated water tank.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.270
It's so important,

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.390
because they hadn't had
clean water in years

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.700
and we have a bunch of schools in Africa

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.140
on our list this year,

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.037
and our 10th anniversary book,

00:01:57.037 --> 00:01:59.220
"One Piece of Paper at a Time" is out.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.650
- Oh, my gosh. That's
incredible, you guys.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.690
I love what you're doing
for all those little babies.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.250
Oh, and that picture. That's so cool.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:08.010
Like you're so young to
be doing such rad stuff.

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:09.570
Thank you for showing everybody

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:10.950
that it's possible
(audience applauding)

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.510
to make simple like,
(audience applauding)

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:16.080
but really effective
change that's necessary.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.490
Thank you so much, Isabelle.

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.810
Thank you so much, Katherine.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.555
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:20.555 --> 00:02:21.388
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:02:21.388 --> 00:02:22.770
- [Isabelle] Thank you.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:23.603
- That's not all.

00:02:23.603 --> 00:02:24.810
Our season long partner Pilot,

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:25.800
pen makers of friction,

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.720
the go-to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.030
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.950
and impacting the world in big ways,

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:32.850
just like y'all.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.850
So, they're gonna give
Paper for Water a $1000.

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:36.921
How's that sound?

00:02:36.921 --> 00:02:38.558
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:39.391
- Wow.
- Wow.

00:02:39.391 --> 00:02:40.430
- Thank you.

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:41.263
- That's amazing.

00:02:41.263 --> 00:02:42.540
- Absolutely, ladies.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.500
We love what you're doing.
(audience cheering)

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.360
Thank you for joining us again
(audience applauding)

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.890
and thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.290
Wilma Valderama, Scott
Horn and Kate the chemist.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.123
Y'all have a great day,
(audience cheering)

00:02:50.123 --> 00:02:51.713
and if it's not, try and change it.

